scenario ser-different-victim
title "Serializable: a different transaction is aborted"
story "T1 reads p:3 (absent) and T3 writes q:2, different keys. This engine sees no dependency, so T2's write to q:1, which waits for T1, fails as a concurrent update once T1 commits. PostgreSQL aborts T1 at commit instead: its read locks are per index page, and p:3 and q:2 share one."
schedule:
  T3 BEGIN
  T1 BEGIN
  T1 PUT q:1 = 51
  T1 READ p:3 AS v1_1
  T3 PUT q:2 = 92
  T3 COMMIT
  T2 BEGIN
  T2 SCAN q: AS v2_2
  T2 PUT q:1 = 1
  T1 COMMIT
  T2 ABORT
